</style>
</head><body>
<div class="meta">Love &amp; Love YAH &middot; Archive</div>
<h1>Prophetic Words</h1>
<p class="lede">The original forty daily prophetic words written for the Daily Prophetic Word page, kept here as a reference copy. Each entry pairs the word with a Scripture, a prayer, and one thing to carry into the day.</p>
<div class="rule"></div>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 01</div>
  <p class="word">The ground you have been praying over is not barren. What you planted in the quiet season is rooting deeper than you can see, and this is the month the roots find water. Do not trade a slow harvest for a fast one.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;For he will be as a tree planted by the waters, who spreads out its roots by the river.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Jeremiah 17:8 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Father, give me the patience of a farmer. Teach me to water what You planted and to wait without striving.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Name one thing you have been tempted to abandon early. Give it one more week of prayer before you decide.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 02</div>
  <p class="word">He is not asking you to be loud. He is asking you to be steady where He put you. Faithfulness in a small room is not a demotion.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;And that you make it your ambition to lead a quiet life, and to do your own business, and to work with your own hands.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">1 Thessalonians 4:11 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Lord, quiet the part of me that needs to be seen. Let my work speak and let You get the credit.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Do one unseen thing well today and tell no one about it.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 03</div>
  <p class="word">The door you knocked on last year is not the door He is opening. Turn around and look. What He is doing now will not fit the shape of what you asked for.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Behold, I will do a new thing. It springs forth now. Don't you know it?&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Isaiah 43:19 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">God, loosen my grip on the old request. Give me eyes for the thing You are actually doing.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Write down the request you have been repeating. Ask Him what He wants to give you instead.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 04</div>
  <p class="word">Forgive the person you keep rehearsing in your mind. That rehearsal is the weight, not the person. You are carrying a conversation that ended a long time ago.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Bearing with one another, and forgiving each other, if any man has a complaint against anyone; even as Christ forgave you, so you also do.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Colossians 3:13 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Father, I release what I have been holding. Take the script out of my mouth and the bitterness out of my chest.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">When the rehearsal starts today, say their name in a blessing instead.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 05</div>
  <p class="word">Provision is already on the road. Keep your hands open and your mouth grateful. What arrives will look ordinary before it looks like a miracle.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;My God will supply every need of yours according to his riches in glory in Christ Jesus.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Philippians 4:19 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Lord, thank You for what is already coming. Keep me thankful before it arrives, not only after.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Thank Him out loud for one thing you do not have yet.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 06</div>
  <p class="word">Stop asking Him to bless a plan you have not surrendered. Bring the whole thing, including the part you were going to keep.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Commit your deeds to God, and your plans shall succeed.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Proverbs 16:3 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">God, here is all of it. Change what needs changing before I build another day on it.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Say out loud the part of your plan you have been protecting from Him.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 07</div>
  <p class="word">Your prayers for your family are not lost. He keeps every one of them. What you prayed at midnight is still on the altar.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Golden bowls full of incense, which are the prayers of the saints.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Revelation 5:8 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Father, remember the prayers I no longer have words for. Answer them in Your time and Your way.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Pray one sentence for someone in your family who does not know you are praying.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 08</div>
  <p class="word">The delay is not a denial and it is not a punishment. He is building the person who can carry the answer.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Let us not be weary in doing good, for we will reap in due season, if we don't give up.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Galatians 6:9 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Lord, do the work in me that the answer requires. I would rather be ready than early.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Ask Him what He is forming in you while you wait, and write down what comes.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 09</div>
  <p class="word">You have been apologizing for taking up space in a room He assigned you. Stand where you are placed. Humility is not the same as hiding.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;God has not given us a spirit of fear, but of power, love, and self-control.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">2 Timothy 1:7 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">God, take the fear out of my voice. Let me be gentle and unafraid at the same time.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Say the one true thing you have been swallowing in a meeting or conversation today.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 10</div>
  <p class="word">Guard the first hour. What gets your attention first will set the tone for everything after it, and the enemy knows this better than you do.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;In the morning, my prayer comes before you.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Psalm 88:13 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Father, You get the first word today. Quiet every other voice until I have heard Yours.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Give Him the first ten minutes tomorrow before you touch your phone.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 11</div>
  <p class="word">The friendship that went quiet is not your failure to fix. Some seasons close so that both of you can grow in soil the other could not give.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;For everything there is a season, and a time for every purpose under heaven.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Ecclesiastes 3:1 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Lord, heal what I cannot repair. Bless them where they are and free me from the replay.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Bless that person in prayer and then leave the outcome alone.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 12</div>
  <p class="word">He is not impressed by your exhaustion. Rest is obedience, and you have been calling your fear of stopping diligence.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Come to me, all you who labor and are heavily burdened, and I will give you rest.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Matthew 11:28 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">God, teach me to stop without guilt. Show me what I am afraid will fall apart if I rest.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Put one thing down today and do not pick it back up until tomorrow.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 13</div>
  <p class="word">The thing you keep starting over is not a curse. You are learning a discipline, not failing a test. Begin again today without the speech about yesterday.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;His compassions don't fail. They are new every morning.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Lamentations 3:22-23 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Father, thank You for mercy that does not run out. Let me begin again without shame.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Restart the one habit you quit, at the smallest possible size.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 14</div>
  <p class="word">Speak to your household. What you say over your home builds it or dismantles it, and the words are landing whether anyone answers or not.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Death and life are in the power of the tongue; those who love it will eat its fruit.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Proverbs 18:21 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Lord, put a guard on my mouth in my own house. Let my family hear life from me.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Say one specific blessing out loud over each person you live with.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 15</div>
  <p class="word">You are not behind. You have been comparing your season to someone else's harvest and calling the difference failure.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Each man should test his own work. Then he will have reason for boasting in himself, and not in someone else.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Galatians 6:4 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">God, take my eyes off the other row. Show me what faithfulness looks like in mine.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Unfollow or mute the one feed that keeps feeding the comparison.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 16</div>
  <p class="word">The wound you keep explaining is asking to be healed, not defended. Bring it to Him before you bring it to another audience.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;He heals the broken in heart, and binds up their wounds.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Psalm 147:3 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Father, I stop building my case. Come into the part of the story I keep telling and heal it.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Tell Him the version of the story you have never said out loud.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 17</div>
  <p class="word">Generosity is your way out of the fear you have been managing. You cannot budget your way to peace, but you can give your way out of scarcity.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Give, and it will be given to you: good measure, pressed down, shaken together, and running over.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Luke 6:38 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Lord, break the grip of scarcity on me. Show me who to give to this week.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Give something away today that you would rather keep.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 18</div>
  <p class="word">The correction you have been avoiding is a kindness. He is not humiliating you. He is removing what would have cost you more later.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;For whom God loves, he disciplines, and chastises every son whom he receives.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Hebrews 12:6 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">God, I receive it. Show me what to change and give me the humility to change it quickly.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Take the correction you have been arguing with and act on one part of it.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 19</div>
  <p class="word">Fear has been doing your planning. Notice how many of your decisions this year began with what might go wrong.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;There is no fear in love; but perfect love casts out fear.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">1 John 4:18 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Father, replace the voice of fear with Your voice. Let love make my decisions from here.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Name one decision fear made for you. Ask Him what love would decide.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 20</div>
  <p class="word">Your obedience does not require an explanation. He has told you enough to take the next step, and He will explain the rest on the road.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Trust in God with all your heart, and don't lean on your own understanding.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Proverbs 3:5 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Lord, I will move on what I know. Keep me from waiting on details You never promised.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Take the one step you already know to take, before you understand step two.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 21</div>
  <p class="word">The gift you buried out of caution is still yours to use. He did not give it to you for a safer season.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;For this cause I remind you that you should stir up the gift of God which is in you.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">2 Timothy 1:6 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">God, stir what I let go cold. Give me a small place to use it again this week.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Use the buried gift once today, badly if necessary.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 22</div>
  <p class="word">Peace is not the absence of the storm. He is offering you peace inside a situation He has not yet changed, and that peace will guard your thinking.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;The peace of God, which surpasses all understanding, will guard your hearts and your thoughts in Christ Jesus.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Philippians 4:7 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Father, guard my mind today. Give me peace that does not depend on the outcome.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">When the anxious thought returns, pray the situation once instead of rehearsing it.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 23</div>
  <p class="word">He is asking for honesty, not performance. The prayer you think is too raw to pray is the one He has been waiting for.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Pour out your heart before him. God is a refuge for us.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Psalm 62:8 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Lord, here is what I actually feel. I trust You with the unpolished version.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Pray one honest, unedited sentence today.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 24</div>
  <p class="word">Do not despise the small beginning. What starts this week will look unimpressive on purpose, so that you know who built it.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Who despises this day of small things?&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Zechariah 4:10 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">God, help me honor the small start. Keep me from needing it to look big to be worth doing.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Begin the small version of the thing you have been waiting to launch.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 25</div>
  <p class="word">The person you are avoiding is part of your healing. You do not have to trust them again to release them.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;If it is possible, as much as it is up to you, be at peace with all men.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Romans 12:18 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Father, give me wisdom about proximity and freedom about resentment. Guard my heart without hardening it.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Decide, in prayer, what peace with that person looks like from your side only.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 26</div>
  <p class="word">You keep asking for a sign and He keeps sending people. Pay attention to who He has already put beside you.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Two are better than one, because they have a good reward for their labor.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Ecclesiastes 4:9 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Lord, thank You for the people You sent. Help me receive help without embarrassment.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Ask one person for the specific help you have been praying for.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 27</div>
  <p class="word">Your worship is not for a good week. It is a weapon in a hard one, and it changes the room before it changes the circumstance.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;About midnight Paul and Silas were praying and singing hymns to God, and the prisoners were listening to them.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Acts 16:25 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">God, I will praise You before anything changes. Let worship be my first response today.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Sing or play one song of worship in the middle of the hardest part of your day.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 28</div>
  <p class="word">Stop negotiating with the thing you already know to leave. Clarity came a while ago; what you are waiting on now is courage.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Therefore let's also lay aside every weight and the sin which so easily entangles us, and let's run with patience the race that is set before us.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Hebrews 12:1 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Father, give me the courage to match the clarity You already gave me.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Set a date for the thing you know you need to end, and tell one person.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 29</div>
  <p class="word">He sees the effort no one has thanked you for. Your reward is not tied to their acknowledgment.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Whatever you do, work heartily, as for the Lord, and not for men.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Colossians 3:23 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Lord, I do this for You. Free me from needing the credit to keep going.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Do the thankless work today as an act of worship and let it be enough.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 30</div>
  <p class="word">The fear about your children is not prophecy. Pray what you want to see over them instead of describing what you dread.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;All your children shall be taught by God, and your children's peace shall be great.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Isaiah 54:13 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Father, I refuse to pray my fears over them. I pray Your promises instead.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Replace one fear about your child with a promise, and pray that promise by name.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 31</div>
  <p class="word">You are allowed to grieve and still trust Him. He is not asking you to pretend the loss was small.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Blessed are those who mourn, for they shall be comforted.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Matthew 5:4 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">God, meet me in the grief. I do not need it explained; I need You near.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Give the grief twenty honest minutes today instead of pushing it down.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 32</div>
  <p class="word">Discipline in your body is not vanity. He is asking you to steward the house you live in, gently and consistently.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Or don't you know that your body is a temple of the Holy Spirit who is in you?&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">1 Corinthians 6:19 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Lord, teach me to care for this body without shame or obsession.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Do one small, kind, physical thing for your body today and repeat it tomorrow.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 33</div>
  <p class="word">The influence you asked for is arriving through service, not position. Take the low seat on purpose and watch what He does with it.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Whoever desires to become great among you shall be your servant.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Matthew 20:26 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Father, make me useful before You make me visible.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Serve in a way that will not be recorded anywhere.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 34</div>
  <p class="word">Your finances need an honest conversation, not a miracle you keep waiting on. He blesses truth about numbers.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Know well the condition of your flocks, and pay attention to your herds.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Proverbs 27:23 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">God, give me courage to look at the real numbers and wisdom for the next step.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Look at the account you have been avoiding and write down the actual figure.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 35</div>
  <p class="word">He is closing a chapter you keep trying to reopen. Let the ending be an ending; there is nothing left in that room for you.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Don't remember the former things, and don't consider the things of old.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Isaiah 43:18 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Lord, help me stop knocking on a closed door. Turn my face toward what is next.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Delete the draft, message, or plan that keeps you tethered to the old chapter.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 36</div>
  <p class="word">Rest is not the reward for finishing. He built it into the week on purpose, and the work will still be there.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Remember the Sabbath day, to keep it holy.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Exodus 20:8 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Father, teach me to keep a day. Show me what I am afraid to trust You with.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Choose your day off this week and protect it before anything else claims it.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 37</div>
  <p class="word">The prayer you gave up on is still open before Him. Nothing you prayed in faith has been thrown away.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;This is the boldness which we have toward him, that if we ask anything according to his will, he listens to us.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">1 John 5:14 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">God, I pick it back up. I trust You with the timing and the answer.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Pray the abandoned prayer once more, out loud.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 38</div>
  <p class="word">You have been treating a spiritual weight as a scheduling problem. Some of what is heavy this week will not move by better planning.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;For our wrestling is not against flesh and blood, but against the principalities, against the powers.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Ephesians 6:12 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Lord, show me what is actually happening. Give me discernment instead of another system.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Fast something small today and pray over the situation instead.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 39</div>
  <p class="word">Tell the truth in the place you have been managing perceptions. The relief on the other side of honesty is worth the discomfort.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;Speaking truth in love, we may grow up in all things into him.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Ephesians 4:15 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">Father, give me words that are both honest and kind. Take the fear out of the conversation.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Have the conversation you have been rehearsing, today, gently.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="entry">
  <div class="num">Word 40</div>
  <p class="word">He has not changed His mind about you. What you did last week did not disqualify you from what He called you to.</p>
  <div class="sub">
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Scripture</div><p class="txt">&ldquo;For the gifts and the calling of God are irrevocable.&rdquo;</p><div class="ref">Romans 11:29 &middot; WEB</div></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Prayer</div><p class="txt">God, thank You that Your call does not depend on my performance. Restore me and send me back.</p></div>
    <div class="block"><div class="lbl">Carry it today</div><p class="txt">Return to the thing you stepped away from in shame, and do the next small part of it.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<p class="colophon">Scripture quotations are taken from the World English Bible (WEB), a public domain modern English translation of the Holy Bible. No permission is required for its use. House style renders the divine name as &ldquo;God&rdquo;; &ldquo;Lord&rdquo; and &ldquo;LORD&rdquo; appear as in the text.</p>
</body></html>